# Everything the image must not carry. The first two entries are the ones that
# matter most: `node_modules` from a Windows host is the wrong platform's binaries,
# and `.env` holds the bot token, the JWT secret and the database password - a
# secret baked into an image layer survives every later attempt to remove it.
node_modules
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

dist
coverage
*.log

.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Tunnel credentials: a bearer credential for the Cloudflare tunnel, mounted into
# cloudflared at runtime and never part of the API image.
docker/cloudflared

# Documentation and tests are not needed to run the service. Tests deliberately so:
# `pnpm test` runs on a developer machine and in CI, not from the runtime image.
*.md
docs
**/*.spec.ts
